{
  "$comment": [
    "The allowlisted source registry (M24). Data, not code: adding a source is a",
    "review of this file, not a deploy of new logic.",
    "",
    "Two deliberate properties of this list:",
    "",
    "1. It includes many outlets that carry the same wire services (PTI, ANI).",
    "   That is the point. Origin clustering has to have real duplicates to collapse,",
    "   and the M26 gate requires at least one multi-outlet cluster in the live",
    "   corpus. Subscribing to outlets that reprint the same wire is a feed-selection",
    "   decision, not synthetic data.",
    "",
    "2. Fact-checkers are marked source_class 'factchecker' and are the only sources",
    "   whose output can become Tier C evidence. News outlets are corroboration",
    "   material; they are not adjudications.",
    "",
    "'allowed_for_primary_check' marks domains whose own pages can settle an",
    "attribution question. It is false by default and set only for bodies that",
    "publish primary records."
  ],
